# Copy to vortexia.env (gitignored — it holds secrets) and fill in what you
# need. Loaded automatically on every start — manual (`node src/index.js
# start`) AND launchd-managed (`launchctl` service) — so vortex-relay config
# survives `install-service.sh` handing vortexia off to launchd, which does
# NOT inherit a shell's `export`ed variables. An explicit shell export still
# takes priority over this file, so nothing changes for a quick manual test.
#
# See docs/vortex-relay-poc.md for how to provision a Gist token or a Nostr
# key. Leave everything commented out for single-Mac mode (no cross-machine
# messaging, vortexia runs exactly as it always has).

# This environment's name — must be unique across every Mac in the society,
# and match what other environments list in their VORTEXIA_RELAY_ENV_NAMES.
# VORTEXIA_ENV_NAME=

# At least one transport below is required once VORTEXIA_ENV_NAME is set.
# Nostr needs no external account (self-generated keypair, free public
# relays, no rate limit shared with other writers) — prefer it over Gist
# unless you specifically need Gist's transport.

# Nostr transport (recommended):
# VORTEXIA_NOSTR_SECRET_KEY=<hex-encoded secret key — nostr-tools generateSecretKey/bytesToHex>
# VORTEXIA_NOSTR_PEERS=<envName>:<pubkeyHex>,<envName2>:<pubkeyHex2>

# Gist transport (GitHub-account-based, 100 writes/hour shared across every
# writer on the token):
# VORTEXIA_GIST_ID=
# VORTEXIA_GIST_TOKEN=

# Every environment expected to publish to the shared directory, comma
# separated. This environment's own name is added automatically if omitted.
# VORTEXIA_RELAY_ENV_NAMES=

# Same-LAN peer discovery (mDNS) — on by default once VORTEXIA_ENV_NAME is
# set; disable only if it's causing trouble on your network.
# VORTEXIA_LAN_DISCOVERY=0
